# Supabase connection settings — copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values.
# Get both values from: Supabase Dashboard -> your project -> Project Settings -> API
# Do NOT commit .env to version control, and do not paste keys into chat.

# The code accepts BOTH naming conventions. Primary (matches the current dashboard):
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# The Vite frontend maps these two names automatically (see vite.config.ts) —
# no separate VITE_* lines are needed.

# Classic aliases also accepted automatically:
#   SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY,
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL, VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#
# The publishable key ("anon" in older projects) is safe for browsers by design;
# Row Level Security is what actually protects your data.

# ⚠️ SERVER-ONLY. Bypasses Row Level Security. Never put this in browser code,
# never commit it, never send it through chat. Leave commented out unless you
# explicitly need server-side admin access:
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
